WEBVTT

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.431
Choose Help, then Demo Projects.

00:00:05.431 --> 00:00:07.663
Each one holds real public data.

00:00:07.663 --> 00:00:12.892
Find Human Mapping and Variants, with results, and click Download and Open.

00:00:12.892 --> 00:00:15.124
You need an internet connection.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:18.786
A project is one folder on your Mac.

00:00:18.786 --> 00:00:21.994
The sidebar on the left shows what is inside.

00:00:21.994 --> 00:00:26.627
Imports holds the reads, short pieces of DNA read by a sequencer.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.059
Click HG002 under Imports.

00:00:30.059 --> 00:00:33.667
These are reads from one anonymous human volunteer.

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:39.538
The Inspector on the right shows how many reads there are and their quality scores.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:45.196
Results go under Analyses, and these were made in advance.

00:00:45.196 --> 00:00:47.732
Open the minimap2 result and zoom in.

00:00:47.732 --> 00:00:53.078
Each read sits where it matches the reference, a slice of human chromosome 20.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.817
Click Operations in the toolbar.

00:01:00.817 --> 00:01:07.409
The Operations Panel lists every task the app runs, like this download, and whether it finished.

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:13.294
To learn more about projects, read the manual chapter The Lungfish Project.

00:01:13.294 --> 00:01:16.410
More videos are on the Videos page of the website.
